        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">Jacque Montague Raymer has announced the availability of a major new release of <a href="makulu">MakuluLinux</a>, a Debian-based desktop Linux distribution with deeply integrated artificial intelligence features: "<span class="Quote">Every other Linux distro gives you an AI plugin. A chatbox. A sidebar widget. Something you open, use once, and close. AI-OS is different. The artificial intelligence isn't a feature - it's the spine of the entire operating system. Every part of the desktop, every workflow, every task you perform has AI woven directly into it. From the moment you boot, you have a full-stack intelligent assistant that knows your system, remembers your history, speaks your language, and executes your intentions. Type one sentence and watch your computer manage itself. That's AI-OS. At the top of the screen, always visible, always ready. The Electra Bar is a floating AI input widget that sits quietly on your desktop. One sentence. Press Enter. The right thing happens, every time. The Electra Bar feeds every input through an intelligent routing agent, a built-in AI that reads your intent and automatically decides what to do. Writing a blog post? It opens Writer mode. Debugging code? Coder mode. Changing WiFi? Command mode. Asking a question? Chat mode.</span>" Read the rest of the <a href="https://makululinux.us/aios-release-notes.html">release notes</a> for more details. <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/makulu/files/downloads/AIOS/">Download (MD5)</a>: <a href="https://sourceforge.net/projects/makulu/files/downloads/AIOS/MakuluLinux-AI-OS-Debian-2026-07-28.iso">MakuluLinux-AI-OS-Debian-2026-07-28.iso</a> (5,209MB, <a href="table.php?distribution=makulu&pkglist=true&version=2026-07-28#pkglist">pkglist</a>).</td>
