        <td class="NewsText" style="font-size: 15px">Saeed Badreldin has announced the release of <a href="helwan">Helwan</a> Linux 5.0, a significant update of the project's Arch-based distribution designed primarily for developers: "<span class="Quote">We are proud to announce the launch of Helwan Linux 5.0, a version that marks a qualitative leap in our distribution philosophy and development. What's new in Helwan Linux 5.0? Integrated technical identity - we have further refined our collection of powerful system tools, ensuring a more seamless and stable integration for developers. Revolutionary update system - we officially announce the end of the 'reinstall' era. Thanks to the infrastructure of Helwan Linux 5.0, users will no longer need to wipe their system or perform a clean install when major new versions are released. Continuous evolution - the new release supports seamless upgrades; your current system will evolve into the latest version-complete with all new programs and innovative features without compromising your data or settings. Developer-centric experience - we have integrated productivity tools, such as Copy Path, Force Kill, and advanced process management directly into the Nemo file manager, to accelerate your development workflow.</span>" Visit the distribution's <a href="https://helwan-linux.github.io/helwanlinux/news.html">news page</a> to read the release announcement. <a href="https://helwan-linux.github.io/helwanlinux/download.html">Download (SHA512)</a>: <a href="https://archive.org/download/helwan-linux-dev-lts-v-5.0-x-86-64/Helwan-Linux-Dev-LTS-v5.0-x86_64.iso">Helwan-Linux-Dev-LTS-v5.0-x86_64.iso</a> (5,940MB, <a href="https://helwan-linux.github.io/helwanlinux/sigs/dev5/Helwan-Linux-Dev-LTS-v5.0-x86_64.iso.sig">signature</a>, <a href="https://archive.org/download/helwan-linux-dev-lts-v-5.0-x-86-64/helwan-linux-dev-lts-v-5.0-x-86-64_archive.torrent">torrent</a>, <a href="table.php?distribution=helwan&amp;pkglist=true&amp;version=5.0#pk